    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Odometer verification against the LR bilty</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The odometer reading displayed on the instrument cluster is read to the nearest kilometre, recorded, and cross‑checked with the mileage printed on the Load Receipt (LR) bilty. A variance greater than the agreed tolerance (usually ±5 km) triggers an investigation, and the discrepancy is documented in the handover report.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Signed condition sign‑off</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Once the visual and mileage checks are satisfied, the receiver signs the condition acknowledgment form. The signature confirms that the vehicle’s exterior, accessories, and odometer reading match the documented state. A copy of the signed form, along with the inspection photos, is filed with the logistics record for future reference.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Documentation and digital archiving</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">All inspection photos, the signed condition sheet, and the LR bilty are scanned or uploaded to the transport management system within 24 hours. The digital file is indexed by vehicle identification number (VIN) and delivery reference, ensuring quick retrieval for audits or warranty queries.</p>
  </div>
</div>
<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">In practice, the handover follows a repeatable sequence: (a) retrieve the pickup photo set and LR bilty, (b) perform the daylight re‑inspection, (c) record the odometer, (d) resolve any discrepancies on site, (e) obtain the recipient’s signature, and (f) archive all paperwork electronically.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This systematic approach minimizes disputes, protects both the shipper and the consignee, and provides a clear audit trail for any post‑delivery claims.</span></li></ul></div>
